@startuml credentials-lifecycle
left to right direction
title Credential and Optional Registry Lifecycle

state "Issuer" as Issuer
state "Holder" as Holder
state "Registry Administrator" as RegistryAdmin
state "App / Wallet" as Client

state "Direct-issued mode" as DirectIssuedMode {
  state "Base Credential\nissuer + holder + 1..n credential subjects" as DirectCredential
}

state "Optional registry capability\nissuer-operated or third-party/shared" as RegistryCapability {
  state "Registered Credential\nimplements Credential and RegisteredCredential" as RegisteredCredential
  state "Registration metadata\nregistryAdmin + registeredAt + expiresAt + meta" as RegistrationMetadata
}

Issuer --> DirectCredential : issue via custom workflow
Holder --> DirectCredential : Credential_ArchiveAsHolder\n(holder archive, not revocation)

Issuer --> RegisteredCredential : issue/register via custom workflow\nor CredentialRegistryFactory
Holder --> RegisteredCredential : jointly authorize as required
RegisteredCredential --> RegistrationMetadata : exposes separate registry view
RegistryAdmin --> RegistrationMetadata : registration policy, removal,\narchive, expiry, and fees
Client --> RegisteredCredential : project Credential for intrinsic fields
Client --> RegistrationMetadata : project RegisteredCredential\nfor known/disclosed contract

note bottom of DirectCredential
Each CredentialSubject contains typed claims about its optional id.
The list is conceptually 1..n; implementations reject an empty list.
Holder is distinct from every credential subject.
Claims.validFrom / validUntil define intrinsic validity.
Issuer revocation and exact direct-issued stakeholders are deferred.
end note

note bottom of RegistrationMetadata
Registration expiry or removal does not change credential validity.
Precise registry status and lifecycle remain deferred.
end note

@enduml
